<table border="0" width="93%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">              <tr><td width="100%" bgcolor="#15A198"><font face="Arial" size="2" color="white"><b>Thursday, October 19, 2000</b></font></td></tr><tr><td width="100%"><font face="Arial" size="2"><BR><b><u>Gods Story</b></u><br>Due to the fact that the entire GameRealm website is going through a overhaul right now I wanted to post the story here as well to make sure everyone sees it :)<br><br>While wiping the froth of a fresh ale from his mouth, Nile spoke of times of old. &#8220;Aye, twas grand my warriors in battle, not fearing death, but embracing it for the honor of Nile. These are but times in memory, but times I shall see again.&#8221; The clacking of chains against a cage in the background as Mashangi enraged begins to speak &#8220;you fools do you not understand that as your mortal followers bicker amongst themselves the followers of Mashangi only grow stronger. My Mages and warriors slaying mortals in droves. For this is chaos and chaos will prevail.&#8221; In the next chamber Gile notices a large bound container. Using the skills of the king of thieves is able to encourage the tumblers to fall into line and thus receive his prize. <br><br>Gile all excited bellows &#8220;Yes The Book Of Ages&#8221; gaining control of his excitement, he begins to observe the writings of this book. He begins to discover that this is how Tanjin was banished from the realm and this book has the power to bring him back. Gile then daydreams of the bounty that would be his if Tanjin was to return, for setting him free. Gile then leaves the Hall to find a safe place, so as to explore these writings more over. While back in the Hall Charral and Divene discuss how there followers are doing well in their absence as Valian listens in and begins to speak &#8220;aye, the mortals are doing well in their bid to win our approval, a few stray but these few can be dealt with.&#8221; <br><br>Xanos then begins to speak &#8220;we need a way to mark the mortals that wish to follow us for the gifts we give and not for our beliefs.&#8221; Balak butts in &#8220;there is a way. We mark these mortals as 1, 2, or 3, if said mortal makes another infraction they would forfeit any god gifts they received.&#8221; Telsia asks, &#8220;how long will a mortal be marked as such?&#8221; Balak reply&#8217;s for the passing of 7 moons from the last infraction.&#8221; The gods agree this is a just solution for the few that maybe misguided. Meanwhile Gile has discovered the way for Tanjin to return. Gile talking to himself begins to attempt to bring Tanjin back, &#8220;hehe, blasted mages so many things to mix together. Ok magic words, magic words, abbra kadrabra?!?!&#8221; that sets off a large explosion. &#8220;Tanjin, you there&#8221;, as Gile peeks through the cloud of smoke with his charred face from the explosion. &#8220;well that didn&#8217;t work.&#8221; Gile proceeds to mix another batch and tries different words of magic. &#8220;Lets see here, words I&#8217;m looking for must be here somewhere? These look like magic words.&#8221; Gile begins rubbing his hands together while chanting &#8220;ablakck, briskov, roglkx.&#8221; Another explosion ensues. From the smoke this time arises Tanjin. With fire flying from his finger tips, in a voice that would shake any realm &#8220;YOUNG GODS!!!!!!!!!!!!&#8221; <br><br>Gile feeling this is no time to ask for a reward decides to make a run for it. Tanjin yells, &#8220;halt young one!!&#8221; Gile feeling that opportunity is knocking begins to tell Tanjin his story. &#8220;Tanjin, first let me say tis great to see thee amongst the realm again. Twas I who freed you from the bond the other gods had imprisoned you. All I seek in return is you guidance or a small gift, hehe.&#8221; Tanjin responds &#8220;aye a gift worthy of my freedom young one. Here is your gift you fool.&#8221; Fire and lightning flowed from Tanjin, striking Gile down. &#8220;Let this be a lesson to you and your young gods, thee cross the ZC and the Elder Gods again it shall be your last.&#8221; Gile, gasping for air feeling it may be his last, reaches for his backback and an elixer of health. Feeling the taste of the elixer brings a sigh of relief. Gile begins to talk to himself, &#8220;well that did not go as planned at all, hehe. I think I need a vacation, someplace nice and warm. I think I shall make my way back to the mortal realm where thee be less chance I will be in need of an elixer&#8221;. Eliane, Kyria and Rocilas discuss their followers when they hear Tanjin&#8217;s voice echo. Startled Eliane voices concern, &#8220;could that be? No&#8230;&#8230;.but&#8230;&#8230;how&#8230;..?&#8221; <br><br>Rocilas calls for all the gods to meet, &#8220;where is Gile?&#8221; Gile still a little dazed returns the Book of Ages to where he found it. Kyria asks, &#8220;where have you been Gile?&#8221; noticing he looks like he has been in battle. Gile responds, &#8220;well&#8230;&#8230;I may have accidentally freed Tanjin&#8221;. <br><br>Balak enraged, &#8220;WHAT!!!!!!!!! Are you mad, do you have any idea what he can or will do to us??&#8221; Gile responds &#8220; I think I have a little idea, hehe. That old timer almost killed me, I was lucky to escape alive.&#8221; Balak lunges at Gile, as Valian steps between the two, &#8220;now settle down Balak, what is done is done, let see what we might learn from this and the old gods.&#8221; After a lengthy discussion the gods decide it is best to see what can be learned from the old gods and not dwell on the past. While this takes place Tanjin calls for the ZC, &#8220;Tarus I have not been in the realm in some time.&#8221; &#8220;Aye m&#8217;lord.&#8221; &#8220;The ZC will no longer do the bidding of the young gods. The ZC will be restored to their rightful place as followers of the old gods. Let the mortal realm on Raven&#8217;s Dust know that this is the hunting grounds of the ZC and as such the mortals that hunt there may become the hunted.&#8221; <br><br>As this takes place Xanos makes plans of his own, &#8220;I shall see the mortal realm be mine at last, Gile the fool has given me the chance to unleash my plan&#8221; What lies ahead for the mortal realm? Only time shall tell. The last that is heard is Xanos, in a haunting laugh &#8220;Muhahahaha, the Age of Xanos nears&#8221;</font></td></tr></table><p>
<a name="newsitem971908787,82747,"></a>
<table border="0" width="93%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">              <tr><td width="100%" bgcolor="#15A198"><font face="Arial" size="2" color="white"><b>Wednesday, October 18, 2000</b></font></td></tr><tr><td width="100%"><font face="Arial" size="2"><BR><b><u>No Character Transfers</b></u><br>GameRealm will no longer accept Character transfers, nor will we allow any Characters to transfer off. This is a standard Server policy for all online games and we felt it was in the best interest of GameRealm and our players to put a stop to it now.</font></td></tr></table><p>
